From 67a988c70caa277cafcca02af30e5a52d9a909fa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: A2Tools-patch <patch@localhost>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 22:53:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Plugins: Twitch and YouTube videos in a widget, played by mpv
 (permission video)

A plugin with the permission "video" plays a Twitch channel or a YouTube
video in one of its widgets (a2.video.play): libmpv, loaded at run time,
draws it into a GL area under the widget's page (a GTK overlay), so the
video is an overlay like the others: above the game, and click-through
while the meter is locked. Only a Twitch channel's or a YouTube video's
address, built from the name or id, is handed to mpv; mpv and yt-dlp
fetch the stream as the player's own mpv would.

The lists: Twitch's public API (gql.twitch.tv, fixed queries, read only,
no account), YouTube's search through yt-dlp, a channel's public feed
(www.youtube.com/feeds/videos.xml), FreeTube's subscriptions from its own
file on this computer (read only), and their pictures (a2.web.image:
i.ytimg.com, yt3.ggpht.com, static-cdn.jtvnw.net). For the Streams plugin.
mpv and yt-dlp are optional dependencies of the package.
